.TH LOG_ERROR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
log_error \- emit a log line at ERROR level with a backtrace
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clogger.h>

log_error(clog lg, const char *fmt, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Expands to a call to _clog_write() at CLOG_ERROR level with automatic
source location capture. After writing the structured log line, a
stack backtrace is appended as tab-indented continuation lines:

  ts=... level=ERROR src=file.c:42 func=handle msg="db timeout"
  \et#0 ./myapp(handle+0x1a) [0x7f...]
  \et#1 ./myapp(main+0x42) [0x7f...]

The continuation lines do not start with "ts=", allowing log
aggregators to group them with the preceding ERROR record.

Backtrace frames 0 and 1 (internal logger frames) are skipped so
that frame #0 is the caller of log_error. Backtrace depth is capped
at 64 frames.

Backtrace requires the binary to be linked with -rdynamic for symbol
resolution. On platforms without execinfo.h, or on a transient
allocation failure while resolving symbol names, capture itself
fails; the log line is still emitted normally, but a single
"\et#error backtrace unavailable" continuation line is appended in
place of the usual per-frame lines so the omission is visible rather
than silent.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
lg     Logger handle (clog).
fmt    printf-style format string.
\&...    Format arguments (optional).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
log_error does NOT terminate the process. Use log_fatal if process
termination is desired.
The backtrace write is also protected by the per-logger mutex, so
the backtrace and the preceding log line always appear contiguously
even under concurrent logging from multiple threads.
Under sustained memory pressure, or when the record's own content
already leaves little room before the internal buffer cap, an
individual backtrace frame that cannot be formatted is omitted (in
favor of any shorter frame that follows) rather than written
incomplete; every line that is written is always a complete,
well-formed record. If none of the frames fit at all, a single
"\et#error backtrace unavailable" continuation line takes their
place, the same marker used when capture itself fails. In
CLOG_FMT_JSON mode, if the backtrace cannot be embedded at all under
such pressure, a "bt_error":"unavailable" key takes the place of "bt"
so the omission is visible rather than silent.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
log_error(lg, "failed to open %s: %s", path, strerror(errno));
log_error(lg, "unexpected state %d in FSM", state);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR log_alert (3),
.BR log_fatal (3),
.BR log_warn (3),
.BR _clog_write (3),
.BR clog_open_fd_mp (3)
